T* (## 11. Security Notes) Tj
T* (Current implementation strengths:) Tj
T* (- JWT-based auth.) Tj
T* (- Role middleware.) Tj
T* (- Session invalidation/support logic.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Hardening recommendations:) Tj
T* (- Replace default JWT secret immediately.) Tj
T* (- Externalize DB credentials and secrets to environment or vault.) Tj
T* (- Restrict CORS and backend direct file access in production.) Tj
T* (- Remove or protect utility/debug scripts before production release.) Tj
T* (- Move to HTTPS-only deployment and secure cookie/session strategy where possible.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## 12. Known Technical Risks) Tj
T* (- Single entry router and dynamic schema expansion may complicate strict change control.) Tj
T* (- Some modules rely on runtime table creation; migration discipline is needed for production.) Tj
T* (- Realtime sidecar is unauthenticated by default on local endpoint and should be network-) Tj
T* (restricted.) Tj
T* (- Logs may include sensitive operational metadata if not rotated/sanitized.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## 13. Suggested Next Engineering Steps) Tj
T* (1. Introduce versioned database migrations as a mandatory deployment gate.) Tj
T* (2. Add OpenAPI/endpoint contract documentation from route modules.) Tj
T* (3. Add CI smoke tests for all role dashboards and critical APIs.) Tj
T* (4. Add centralized secret management + environment-specific config.) Tj
T* (5. Add structured logging sink and retention policy.) Tj
T* () Tj
